#Title M24R-A bounded asynchronous layer transition
#Game Copyright-free SAME backend conformance fixture
#Author SAME
#Timer 64
#ZenLen 192

@0 synthetic_layer_tone

; The first five subroutines are the fixed B-lane entry points consumed by the
; driver patch.  They contain only precompiled TAD bytecode; the runtime table
; schedules admission and never schedules notes.
!b_lane_0 @0 V64 o4 [c%24 r%8 e%24 r%8]64
!b_lane_1 @0 V54 o4 [g%20 r%12 d%20 r%12]64
!b_lane_2 @0 V48 o5 [c%16 r%16 g%16 r%16]64
!b_lane_3 @0 V42 o3 [a%28 r%4 f%28 r%4]64
!b_lane_4 @0 V36 o5 [e%12 r%20 b%12 r%20]64

; Group A occupies all eight physical music voices.  Every note lasts 4,000
; driver ticks, so the deliberately asynchronous request and all five steals
; occur while these streams are inside notes, not at a bytecode selector.
A @0 V48 o2 c%4000
B @0 V48 o2 d%4000
C @0 V48 o2 e%4000
D @0 V48 o2 f%4000
E @0 V48 o2 g%4000
F @0 V48 o2 a%4000
G @0 V48 o2 b%4000
H @0 V48 o3 c%4000
